// NO shadowing (E0059): one name, one meaning, per scope stack. An anonymous closure CAPTURES its
// surrounding scope, so a closure parameter reusing a captured binding's name is rejected — the
// body could no longer say which `base` it means. (A NAMED fn is different: it is sealed — it sees
// no surrounding value bindings unless `use (…)`-captured — so its params conflict with nothing.)
// Assignment never re-declares (it reassigns, E0006/E0007), and `is`-narrowing refines the same
// binding, so shadowing is never needed.
// expect: error E0059 at 10:13
// expect: exit 1
base = 100;
double = fn(base: int) => base * 2;
echo double(5);
